  },
  {
   "k": "1ftjdix",
   "en": "Diplomacy"
  },
  {
   "k": "17gvjz6",
   "en": "Main article: Diplomacy"
  },
  {
   "k": "argeip",
   "en": "Ownership over territory is determined at the state level. Control over both the resources and state-wide construction of a state is determined by the plurality controller of a state, meaning the country that controls the most victory points. Each province in a state is worth 0.1⟦0⟧ victory points. Some provinces (usually cities) have additional victory points.",
   "frags": 1
  },
  {
   "k": "2if98",
   "en": "These are all named and marked with small squares (1 to 9 VPs), pentagons (10 to 15 VPs), circles (20 to 40 VPs), or stars (capitals with 1 to 50 VPs) on the map and their additional victory points are displayed in the tooltip when hovering over them. Resistance is computed at the state level."
  },
  {
   "k": "cuj76f",
   "en": "Cores"
  },
  {
   "k": "73wn8b",
   "en": "States can be either core states or colony states. Cores are considered an integral part of the country, and the inhabitants are fully available for military service. Nations get a ⟦0⟧ penalty to manpower in colony states, and have half as many building slots available as in a core state.",
   "frags": 1
  },
  {
   "k": "o720sa",
   "en": "Nations may justify war goals against foreign-owned core states in half the time and for half the political power as on other states. Only victory points in core states count when determining if a country will capitulate. When a nation controls a non-core state, that state will generate ⟦0⟧.",
   "frags": 1
  },
  {
   "k": "60wqo0",
   "en": "resistance"
  },
  {
   "k": "dp9ft2",
   "en": "Unlike other Paradox games, there is normally no way for countries to gain cores. You can lose cores if you release/return territory of a country."
  },
  {
   "k": "wfleq7",
   "en": "Some country-specific events and national focuses, like the Anschluss event for ⟦0⟧ or decisions for ⟦1⟧ for central America, will grant cores. As of the ⟦2⟧ expansion, there is an exception to this rule, with ⟦3⟧ able to core any state with enough compliance with the Global Defense Council focus.",
   "frags": 4
  },
  {
   "k": "alybni",
   "en": "Germany"
  },
  {
   "k": "cabrx2",
   "en": "Mexico"
